{
  "abstract": "No symmetric incidence configuration exists with 59 points and 59 lines, eight incidences at every point and line, and at most one common line for any two distinct points. The compared declaration states the equivalent binary integer incidence-matrix theorem. It places no restriction on the automorphism group or the cycle types of the leave graphs. The proof derives leave-graph constraints from an arbitrary incidence matrix and closes the resulting finite cases in Lean. Davydov, Faina, Giulietti, Marcugini and Pambianco distinguish this unrestricted case, listed as undecided in their Table 7.1, from the cyclic case in Table 6.1.",
